window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["restful-api"]=[{"id":"restful-api-f0001","card":"q-restful-api-001-1-course-overview-and-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s002","q":"What is Flask?","a":"<p>A Python microframework for web apps and APIs. It gives essential features without forcing infrastructure choices, and has a large plugin ecosystem.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0002","card":"q-restful-api-001-1-course-overview-and-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s002","q":"Why does a REST API return JSON instead of XML or a custom format?","a":"<p>JSON needs no parsing and is supported natively by Python and most languages.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0003","card":"q-restful-api-001-1-course-overview-and-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites for the Flask API course?","a":"<p>Basic Python 3, and how web apps work (form posts, request/response).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0004","card":"q-restful-api-001-1-course-overview-and-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s002","q":"Which tools does the Flask API course use, and for what?","a":"<p><strong>PyCharm</strong> (Professional has Flask tooling; Community works with manual venv/pip), <strong>Postman</strong> to test all HTTP verbs, and <strong>DB Browser for SQLite</strong> to inspect the DB file.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0005","card":"q-restful-api-001-1-course-overview-and-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s002","q":"Why does the Planetary API course use SQLite?","a":"<p>It is file-based and needs no server, which avoids PostgreSQL or MySQL setup.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0006","card":"q-restful-api-002-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s003","q":"Why is the Planetary API backend-only with no UI?","a":"<p>Any client (web, mobile, desktop) can then use it. All testing is done in Postman.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0007","card":"q-restful-api-002-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s003","q":"What features does the Planetary API have?","a":"<p>List planets, register users, authenticate users, and add, update and delete planets (for example, deleting Pluto after reclassification).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0008","card":"q-restful-api-002-the-planetary-api","sec":"restful-api-s003","q":"What data does the Planetary API store?","a":"<p>Planets (name, type, home star, mass, radius, distance) and users (name, email, password).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0009","card":"q-restful-api-003-2-project-setup-first-endpoint-dev-serve","sec":"restful-api-s004","q":"How do you set up the Planetary API project in PyCharm Professional?","a":"<p>New Project, <strong>Flask</strong>, name <code>planetary-api</code>, create a <strong>virtualenv</strong> (default <code>venv/</code>; Conda is the alternative for scientific work), and choose a Python interpreter (3.4+ works). PyCharm generates <code>app.py</code> and installs Flask.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0010","card":"q-restful-api-003-2-project-setup-first-endpoint-dev-serve","sec":"restful-api-s004","q":"What does the PyCharm-created Flask <code>app.py</code> look like?","a":"<p>It creates the app, maps <code>/</code> to a function, and runs under a <code>__main__</code> guard.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask import Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(&#x27;/&#x27;)\ndef hello_world():\n    return &#x27;Hello, World!&#x27;\n\nif __name__ == &#x27;__main__&#x27;:\n    app.run()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0011","card":"q-restful-api-003-2-project-setup-first-endpoint-dev-serve","sec":"restful-api-s004","q":"What do <code>Flask(__name__)</code>, <code>@app.route('/')</code> and the <code>__main__</code> guard do?","a":"<p><code>Flask(__name__)</code> creates the app. <code>@app.route('/')</code> is the decorator that maps a URL (endpoint) to the function. The <code>__main__</code> guard is the entry point.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0012","card":"q-restful-api-003-2-project-setup-first-endpoint-dev-serve","sec":"restful-api-s004","q":"How does the course add a second endpoint <code>/super_simple</code>?","a":"<p>With another <code>@app.route</code> function.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/super_simple&#x27;)\ndef super_simple():\n    return &#x27;Hello from the Planetary API.&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0013","card":"q-restful-api-003-2-project-setup-first-endpoint-dev-serve","sec":"restful-api-s004","q":"In a Flask app, what PEP 8 spacing rule applies when you add a second endpoint?","a":"<p>Leave two blank lines between functions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0014","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"What is the Flask built-in dev server, and is it for production?","a":"<p>It is a Werkzeug server. It is fragile and not for production.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0015","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"How do you start the Planetary API and stop it?","a":"<p>Run <code>python app.py</code>. It serves on localhost:5000, and Ctrl+C stops it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python app.py        # serves on localhost:5000, Ctrl+C to stop</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0016","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"Why use Postman instead of a browser to test an API?","a":"<p>A browser only sends GET. APIs use GET/POST/PUT/DELETE for CRUD. In Postman you check the body, the status (<code>200 OK</code>) and the server log (verb, route, status).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0017","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"How do you enable auto-reload for the Flask dev server in PyCharm?","a":"<p>Set the Run Configuration environment variables <code>FLASK_ENV=development</code> and <code>FLASK_DEBUG=True</code>. Without them, every code change needs a manual restart.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0018","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"Where does configuration such as DB strings and API keys belong?","a":"<p>In environment variables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0019","card":"q-restful-api-004-running-and-testing","sec":"restful-api-s005","q":"Besides <code>python app.py</code>, how can you run a Flask app in PyCharm?","a":"<p>Use a PyCharm Flask-server Run Configuration pointing at <code>app.py</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0020","card":"q-restful-api-005-jsonify","sec":"restful-api-s006","q":"What does Flask <code>jsonify</code> do?","a":"<p>It turns keyword arguments or a dict into a JSON response and sets <code>Content-Type: application/json</code>. Without it, the endpoint returns plain text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return jsonify(message=&quot;Hello from the Planetary API&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0021","card":"q-restful-api-005-jsonify","sec":"restful-api-s006","q":"Can <code>jsonify</code> take several key/value pairs?","a":"<p>Yes. <code>jsonify(message=\"...\", status=\"success\")</code> returns <code>{\"message\": \"...\", \"status\": \"success\"}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0022","card":"q-restful-api-005-jsonify","sec":"restful-api-s006","q":"Why does the Planetary API route use <code>methods=['GET']</code>?","a":"<p>To restrict the route to the GET verb.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/super_simple&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;GET&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0023","card":"q-restful-api-006-http-status-codes","sec":"restful-api-s007","q":"What are HTTP status codes?","a":"<p>Response metadata that says whether the request worked. Clients (web, mobile, desktop) branch on them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0024","card":"q-restful-api-006-http-status-codes","sec":"restful-api-s007","q":"What do 200, 401 and 404 mean, and what are the 400-499 and 500-599 ranges?","a":"<p><strong>200</strong> OK, <strong>401</strong> Unauthorized, <strong>404</strong> Not Found. <strong>400-499</strong> are client errors, <strong>500-599</strong> are server errors.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0025","card":"q-restful-api-006-http-status-codes","sec":"restful-api-s007","q":"How do you return a non-200 status from a Flask handler?","a":"<p>Return a tuple. Flask defaults to 200, and setting 200 explicitly is optional but clearer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return jsonify(message=&quot;That resource was not found&quot;), 404</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0026","card":"q-restful-api-006-http-status-codes","sec":"restful-api-s007","q":"How can a JavaScript client branch on the status of <code>/not_found</code>?","a":"<p>Check <code>response.status</code> in the <code>fetch</code> chain.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>fetch(&#x27;http://localhost:5000/not_found&#x27;)\n    .then(response =&gt; {\n        if (response.status === 200) {\n            return response.json().then(data =&gt; console.log(data));\n        } else if (response.status === 404) {\n            console.log(&#x27;Resource not found&#x27;);\n        } else {\n            console.log(`Error: ${response.status}`);\n        }\n    })\n    .catch(error =&gt; console.error(&#x27;Request failed:&#x27;, error));</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0027","card":"q-restful-api-007-url-query-parameters","sec":"restful-api-s008","q":"How are URL (query) parameters sent and read in Flask?","a":"<p>They are sent after <code>?</code> as key/value pairs, such as <code>?name=Bruce&amp;age=28</code>. Read them with <code>request.args.get('name')</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0028","card":"q-restful-api-007-url-query-parameters","sec":"restful-api-s008","q":"Why must you cast Flask query parameter values?","a":"<p>Values are <strong>strings</strong>, so cast them, for example <code>int(...)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>age = int(request.args.get(&#x27;age&#x27;))   # cast to int</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0029","card":"q-restful-api-007-url-query-parameters","sec":"restful-api-s008","q":"What should an API do with query parameter values?","a":"<p>Business rules stay in the API, so the frontend only builds the URL. Validate missing or non-numeric values, and sanitize anything that reaches a DB query.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0030","card":"q-restful-api-007-url-query-parameters","sec":"restful-api-s008","q":"What does <code>/parameters?name=Bruce&amp;age=28</code> return, and what does <code>age=14</code> return?","a":"<p>The first returns 200 with a welcome message. <code>age=14</code> returns 401.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return jsonify(message=f&quot;Sorry {name}, you are not old enough&quot;), 401</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0031","card":"q-restful-api-007-url-query-parameters","sec":"restful-api-s008","q":"How does a frontend call the <code>/parameters</code> endpoint?","a":"<p>It builds the URL with the name and age.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>fetch(`http://localhost:5000/parameters?name=${name}&amp;age=${age}`)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0032","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"What are URL variables in Flask and why use them?","a":"<p>Parts of the path become variables with <code>&lt;name&gt;</code>. URLs are cleaner (<code>/url_variables/Bruce/28</code> instead of <code>?name=Bruce&amp;age=28</code>) and <code>request.args.get()</code> is not needed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0033","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"What must match between a Flask route and its function?","a":"<p>Variable names in the route must match the function parameters in name and count.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0034","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"What does a Flask converter do, and what are the converters?","a":"<p>It restricts and converts the type, written <code>&lt;converter:variable&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Converter</th><th>Accepts</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>string</code> (default)</td><td>any text without slashes. It is <code>string</code>, not Python's <code>str</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>int</code> / <code>float</code></td><td>numbers, converted automatically</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>path</code></td><td>text including slashes (file paths)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>uuid</td><td>UUID strings</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0035","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"In a Flask route with converters, where do the converter and the type hint go?","a":"<p>In the route the converter comes before the name (<code>int:age</code>). In the signature the type hint comes after (<code>age: int</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/url_variables/&lt;string:name&gt;/&lt;int:age&gt;&#x27;)\ndef url_variables(name: str, age: int):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0036","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"What do <code>/url_variables/Bruce/28</code> and <code>/url_variables/Bruce/14</code> return?","a":"<p>The first returns 200 and the second returns 401.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0037","card":"q-restful-api-008-url-variables-and-conversion-filters","sec":"restful-api-s009","q":"How should you document endpoints with typed URL variables?","a":"<p>Use Swagger/OpenAPI with their expected types.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0038","card":"q-restful-api-009-4-database-with-sqlalchemy-models-and-se","sec":"restful-api-s010","q":"What is an ORM, and what are its benefits?","a":"<p>An <strong>ORM</strong> (SQLAlchemy) generates SQL behind the scenes and represents rows as Python objects. Benefits: no raw SQL, easy database switching (SQLite to MySQL), schema defined in code (version-controlled), and support for several databases when shipping on-premises.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0039","card":"q-restful-api-009-4-database-with-sqlalchemy-models-and-se","sec":"restful-api-s010","q":"Which package do you install for SQLAlchemy in Flask?","a":"<p><strong>Flask-SQLAlchemy</strong>, with the dash. <code>FlaskSQLAlchemy</code> is a different package. It installs <code>SQLAlchemy</code> too.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install Flask-SQLAlchemy</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0040","card":"q-restful-api-009-4-database-with-sqlalchemy-models-and-se","sec":"restful-api-s010","q":"How do you configure a SQLite database in Flask-SQLAlchemy?","a":"<p>Set <code>SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI</code> (spelled exactly) to <code>sqlite:///</code> plus a file path, then initialize <code>SQLAlchemy</code> after config. <code>os.path.join</code> keeps paths cross-platform.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.config[&#x27;SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI&#x27;] = &#x27;sqlite:///&#x27; + os.path.join(basedir, &#x27;planets.db&#x27;)\ndb = SQLAlchemy(app)    # initialize after config</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0041","card":"q-restful-api-009-4-database-with-sqlalchemy-models-and-se","sec":"restful-api-s010","q":"What does SQLite give you in the Planetary API?","a":"<p>A file-based database that needs no server and ships with Python.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0042","card":"q-restful-api-010-orm-models","sec":"restful-api-s011","q":"How do you define a SQLAlchemy model in Flask?","a":"<p>As a class inheriting <code>db.Model</code>, mapped to a table. <code>__tablename__</code> sets the table name and <code>db.Column</code> defines columns.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class User(db.Model):\n    __tablename__ = &#x27;users&#x27;\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    email = db.Column(db.String, unique=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0043","card":"q-restful-api-010-orm-models","sec":"restful-api-s011","q":"What columns does the <code>Planet</code> model have?","a":"<p><code>planet_id</code> as primary key, plus <code>planet_name</code>, <code>planet_type</code>, <code>home_star</code>, and the floats <code>mass</code>, <code>radius</code> and <code>distance</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Planet(db.Model):\n    __tablename__ = &#x27;planets&#x27;\n    planet_id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    mass = db.Column(db.Float)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0044","card":"q-restful-api-010-orm-models","sec":"restful-api-s011","q":"What columns does the <code>User</code> model have?","a":"<p><code>id</code> (primary key), <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>, <code>email</code> (unique) and <code>password</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>first_name = db.Column(db.String)\nlast_name = db.Column(db.String)\npassword = db.Column(db.String)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0045","card":"q-restful-api-010-orm-models","sec":"restful-api-s011","q":"Can Flask-SQLAlchemy models live in separate files?","a":"<p>Yes. Models can live in one file or be split into modules.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0046","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"How do you register a custom Flask CLI command?","a":"<p>Decorate a function with <code>@app.cli.command</code>. The Flask CLI (1.0+) runs it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.cli.command(&#x27;db_create&#x27;)\ndef db_create():\n    db.create_all()\n    print(&#x27;Database created&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0047","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"What do <code>db.create_all()</code> and <code>db.drop_all()</code> do?","a":"<p><code>db.create_all()</code> builds tables from the models. <code>db.drop_all()</code> removes them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.cli.command(&#x27;db_drop&#x27;)\ndef db_drop():\n    db.drop_all()\n    print(&#x27;Database dropped&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0048","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"How do you run the create, seed and drop commands?","a":"<p>From the shell with <code>flask</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>flask db_create\nflask db_seed\nflask db_drop</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0049","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"What do <code>db.session.add()</code> and <code>db.session.commit()</code> do?","a":"<p><code>db.session.add()</code> stages a record and <code>db.session.commit()</code> persists it. Without <code>commit</code>, nothing is saved (the lesson hit this bug).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db.session.add(mercury)\ndb.session.commit()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0050","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"How does the <code>db_seed</code> command create a planet?","a":"<p>It builds a <code>Planet</code> object with its fields.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mercury = Planet(planet_name=&#x27;Mercury&#x27;, planet_type=&#x27;Class D&#x27;, home_star=&#x27;Sol&#x27;,\n                 mass=3.258e23, radius=1516, distance=35.98e6)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0051","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"Which test user does <code>db_seed</code> create?","a":"<p>William Herschel with email <code>test@test.com</code> and password <code>P@ssw0rd</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>test_user = User(first_name=&#x27;William&#x27;, last_name=&#x27;Herschel&#x27;,\n                 email=&#x27;test@test.com&#x27;, password=&#x27;P@ssw0rd&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0052","card":"q-restful-api-011-flask-cli-commands-create-drop-seed","sec":"restful-api-s012","q":"How do you check the seeded data in DB Browser for SQLite?","a":"<p>Open Database, pick <code>planets.db</code>, and check the <code>users</code> and <code>planets</code> tables with Browse Data. It does not auto-refresh, and after <code>db_drop</code> the file can remain with no tables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0053","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"What error appears when a Flask endpoint returns ORM objects directly through <code>jsonify</code>?","a":"<p><code>TypeError: Object of type Planet is not JSON serializable</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return jsonify(data=planets_list)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0054","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"Why can the <code>/planets</code> endpoint return a 500 after the DB was dropped?","a":"<p>The DB was not recreated. Run <code>flask db_create</code> and <code>flask db_seed</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0055","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"What does Marshmallow do, and which package integrates it with Flask?","a":"<p>Marshmallow converts SQLAlchemy objects into JSON-compatible dicts, with no manual loops. <strong>Flask-Marshmallow</strong> integrates it and installs <code>marshmallow</code> too.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install flask-marshmallow</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0056","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"In what order do you initialize SQLAlchemy and Marshmallow?","a":"<p>Initialize Marshmallow after SQLAlchemy.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db = SQLAlchemy(app)\nma = Marshmallow(app)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0057","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"How do you define a Marshmallow schema?","a":"<p>Subclass <code>ma.Schema</code> and list the fields to serialize in <code>Meta</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class UserSchema(ma.Schema):\n    class Meta:\n        fields = (&#x27;id&#x27;, &#x27;first_name&#x27;, &#x27;last_name&#x27;, &#x27;email&#x27;, &#x27;password&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0058","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"How do you make a schema for a list of objects?","a":"<p>Pass <code>many=True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_schema = UserSchema()\nusers_schema = UserSchema(many=True)\nplanet_schema = PlanetSchema()\nplanets_schema = PlanetSchema(many=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0059","card":"q-restful-api-012-5-serialization-with-marshmallow","sec":"restful-api-s013","q":"How does the fixed <code>/planets</code> endpoint serialize results?","a":"<p>It dumps the list through the schema and returns <code>result.data</code>. The <code>dump()</code> result is read via <code>.data</code> in the course's older Marshmallow.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = planets_schema.dump(planets_list)\nreturn jsonify(result.data)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0060","card":"q-restful-api-013-6-crud-endpoints","sec":"restful-api-s014","q":"Which Planetary API CRUD endpoints are open and which are protected?","a":"<p>Read endpoints are open. Create, update and delete are protected by <code>@jwt_required</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0061","card":"q-restful-api-014-read-one-planet-get","sec":"restful-api-s015","q":"How does the Planetary API read one planet?","a":"<p>Query by <code>planet_id</code> and return it through the schema, or 404 if missing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/planet_details/&lt;int:planet_id&gt;&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;GET&#x27;])\ndef planet_details(planet_id: int):\n    planet = Planet.query.filter_by(planet_id=planet_id).first()\n    if planet:\n        result = planet_schema.dump(planet)\n        return jsonify(result.data)\n    return jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;that planet does not exist&quot;}), 404</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0062","card":"q-restful-api-014-read-one-planet-get","sec":"restful-api-s015","q":"What does <code>.first()</code> return when no row matches?","a":"<p><code>None</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0063","card":"q-restful-api-014-read-one-planet-get","sec":"restful-api-s015","q":"What do <code>/planet_details/1</code> and <code>/planet_details/100</code> return?","a":"<p><code>/planet_details/1</code> returns Mercury (200). <code>/planet_details/100</code> returns 404.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0064","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"What are the steps to create a planet in the Planetary API?","a":"<p>Check for a duplicate name (409), read form fields, build a <code>Planet</code>, add and commit, and return 201.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db.session.add(new_planet)\ndb.session.commit()\nreturn jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;You added a planet&quot;}), 201</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0065","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"Where does <code>@jwt_required</code> go relative to <code>@app.route</code>?","a":"<p><strong>Below</strong> <code>@app.route</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/add_planet&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;POST&#x27;])\n@jwt_required\ndef add_planet():</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0066","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"How does <code>add_planet</code> detect a duplicate?","a":"<p>It queries by planet name and returns 409.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>test = Planet.query.filter_by(planet_name=planet_name).first()\nif test:\n    return jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;There is already a planet by that name&quot;}), 409</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0067","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"How do you read and convert form fields in <code>add_planet</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>request.form[...]</code> and cast numbers with <code>float</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>planet_name = request.form[&#x27;planet_name&#x27;]\nmass = float(request.form[&#x27;mass&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0068","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"What happens if you POST to <code>/add_planet</code> without a token, and how do you fix it?","a":"<p>It returns 401 <code>Missing Authorization Header</code>. POST <code>/login</code>, then put the JWT in Postman's Authorization tab as a <strong>Bearer Token</strong>. A valid request returns 201 and a duplicate name returns 409.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0069","card":"q-restful-api-015-create-a-planet-post-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s016","q":"What must match in the Postman form when posting a planet?","a":"<p>The form keys must match the code exactly.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0070","card":"q-restful-api-016-update-a-planet-put-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s017","q":"How does the Planetary API update a planet?","a":"<p>Read <code>planet_id</code> from the form, find the row, assign new attribute values and commit. Success returns 202, a missing planet returns 404.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/update_planet&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;PUT&#x27;])\n@jwt_required\ndef update_planet():\n    planet_id = int(request.form[&#x27;planet_id&#x27;])\n    planet = Planet.query.filter_by(planet_id=planet_id).first()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0071","card":"q-restful-api-016-update-a-planet-put-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s017","q":"Why does update not call <code>db.session.add()</code>?","a":"<p>The object is already tracked by the session, so assigning attributes and calling commit is enough.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>planet.planet_name = request.form[&#x27;planet_name&#x27;]\ndb.session.commit()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0072","card":"q-restful-api-016-update-a-planet-put-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s017","q":"Which verb is the standard for update?","a":"<p>PUT is the standard update verb, but some teams use POST. Supporting both is an option.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0073","card":"q-restful-api-016-update-a-planet-put-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s017","q":"What goes wrong with a typo in a form key, and with an expired token?","a":"<p>A typo such as <code>home_start</code> instead of <code>home_star</code> causes an error. An expired token returns <code>Token has expired</code>, so log in again via <code>/login</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0074","card":"q-restful-api-017-delete-a-planet-delete-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s018","q":"How does the Planetary API delete a planet?","a":"<p>The ID comes from the URL. Find the planet, call <code>db.session.delete()</code> and commit.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/remove_planet/&lt;int:planet_id&gt;&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;DELETE&#x27;])\n@jwt_required\ndef remove_planet(planet_id):\n    planet = Planet.query.filter_by(planet_id=planet_id).first()\n    if planet:\n        db.session.delete(planet)\n        db.session.commit()\n        return jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;you deleted a planet&quot;}), 202\n    return jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;that planet does not exist&quot;}), 404</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0075","card":"q-restful-api-017-delete-a-planet-delete-jwt-protected","sec":"restful-api-s018","q":"Is the Planetary API delete permanent?","a":"<p>Yes, it is a hard delete. Some apps set a \"deleted\" flag instead. <code>/remove_planet/999</code> returns 404.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0076","card":"q-restful-api-018-status-codes-used-in-the-api","sec":"restful-api-s019","q":"Which status codes does the Planetary API use and for what?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Used for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>200</td><td>successful read, login</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>201</td><td>resource created (add planet, register)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>202</td><td>accepted (update, delete)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>401</td><td>missing token or bad credentials</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>404</td><td>planet not found</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>409</td><td>conflict (duplicate planet name or email)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0077","card":"q-restful-api-018-status-codes-used-in-the-api","sec":"restful-api-s019","q":"Which status does the Planetary API return for a duplicate planet name or email?","a":"<p>409.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0078","card":"q-restful-api-019-why-jwt","sec":"restful-api-s020","q":"What do JSON Web Tokens do?","a":"<p>They handle authentication and authorization and keep the API <strong>stateless</strong>. APIs avoid server-side session plugins such as Flask-Login or Flask-User.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0079","card":"q-restful-api-019-why-jwt","sec":"restful-api-s020","q":"Where is JWT supported?","a":"<p>It is an open standard supported across languages, and works for web apps (React, Angular), mobile and desktop clients.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0080","card":"q-restful-api-019-why-jwt","sec":"restful-api-s020","q":"What is the Planetary API login rule?","a":"<p>Login is required to add, edit or delete planets. Login is not required to list planets, view details, or register.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0081","card":"q-restful-api-019-why-jwt","sec":"restful-api-s020","q":"Which library provides JWT in Flask?","a":"<p><code>Flask-JWT-extended</code>. It can be used as a black box; see jwt.io for internals.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0082","card":"q-restful-api-020-register-a-user-post-open","sec":"restful-api-s021","q":"What does the <code>/register</code> endpoint expect, and what does it return?","a":"<p>Form fields <code>email</code>, <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code> and <code>password</code>. A duplicate email returns 409 and success returns 201.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0083","card":"q-restful-api-020-register-a-user-post-open","sec":"restful-api-s021","q":"How does <code>/register</code> check for an existing user?","a":"<p>It queries by email. No Marshmallow is needed for this check.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>test = User.query.filter_by(email=email).first()\nif test:\n    return jsonify(message=&#x27;That email already exists&#x27;), 409</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0084","card":"q-restful-api-020-register-a-user-post-open","sec":"restful-api-s021","q":"What does <code>/register</code> do on success?","a":"<p>It adds the user, commits and returns 201.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db.session.add(user)\ndb.session.commit()\nreturn jsonify(message=&#x27;User created successfully&#x27;), 201</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0085","card":"q-restful-api-020-register-a-user-post-open","sec":"restful-api-s021","q":"What is missing from the minimal register endpoint for real apps?","a":"<p>Validation, <strong>password hashing</strong> and possibly approval workflows. Passwords here are stored in plain text for the demo only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0086","card":"q-restful-api-020-register-a-user-post-open","sec":"restful-api-s021","q":"How do you test <code>/register</code>?","a":"<p>Use a new email (201) and the seeded <code>test@test.com</code> (409).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0087","card":"q-restful-api-021-jwt-setup","sec":"restful-api-s022","q":"How do you set up Flask-JWT-extended?","a":"<p>Import <code>JWTManager</code>, <code>jwt_required</code> and <code>create_access_token</code>, set <code>JWT_SECRET_KEY</code>, and create <code>JWTManager(app)</code>. Change the secret in production (for example, a UUID).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask_jwt_extended import JWTManager, jwt_required, create_access_token\n\napp.config[&#x27;JWT_SECRET_KEY&#x27;] = &#x27;super-secret&#x27;  # change in production (e.g. a UUID)\njwt = JWTManager(app)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0088","card":"q-restful-api-022-login-post-open-issues-the-token","sec":"restful-api-s023","q":"What does the <code>/login</code> endpoint accept and return?","a":"<p>JSON (<code>request.is_json</code>) or form data. A matching email and password returns an <code>access_token</code> (200), otherwise 401.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if request.is_json:\n    email = request.json[&#x27;email&#x27;]\n    password = request.json[&#x27;password&#x27;]\nelse:\n    email = request.form[&#x27;email&#x27;]\n    password = request.form[&#x27;password&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0089","card":"q-restful-api-022-login-post-open-issues-the-token","sec":"restful-api-s023","q":"How does <code>/login</code> create the token?","a":"<p>It looks up the user and calls <code>create_access_token</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>test = User.query.filter_by(email=email, password=password).first()\nif test:\n    access_token = create_access_token(identity=email)\n    return jsonify(message=&#x27;login succeeded&#x27;, access_token=access_token), 200\nelse:\n    return jsonify(message=&#x27;bad email or password&#x27;), 401</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0090","card":"q-restful-api-022-login-post-open-issues-the-token","sec":"restful-api-s023","q":"How does a client send the token to protected routes?","a":"<p>As <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0091","card":"q-restful-api-022-login-post-open-issues-the-token","sec":"restful-api-s023","q":"Why does the Planetary API login endpoint use POST, and is that choice settled?","a":"<p>POST for login is common, though debated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0092","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"Which tools does the lost-password email use?","a":"<p><code>flask-mail</code> plus <strong>Mailtrap</strong>, a fake SMTP inbox for testing. You can inspect headers, HTML and text there.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0093","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"Where do mail credentials belong?","a":"<p>In environment variables (PyCharm Run Configuration or the OS), never in code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.config[&#x27;MAIL_USERNAME&#x27;] = os.environ[&#x27;MAIL_USERNAME&#x27;]\napp.config[&#x27;MAIL_PASSWORD&#x27;] = os.environ[&#x27;MAIL_PASSWORD&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0094","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"How do you configure Flask-Mail with Mailtrap?","a":"<p>Set <code>MAIL_SERVER</code> and credentials, then create <code>Mail(app)</code>. The <code>Mail</code> object must be initialized before the endpoint is used.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.config[&#x27;MAIL_SERVER&#x27;] = &#x27;smtp.mailtrap.io&#x27;\nmail = Mail(app)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0095","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"How does <code>/retrieve_password/&lt;email&gt;</code> send the email?","a":"<p>It finds the user, builds a <code>Message</code> and calls <code>mail.send</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>msg = Message(\n    &#x27;Your planetary API password is &#x27; + user.password,\n    sender=&#x27;admin@planetary-api.com&#x27;,\n    recipients=[email]\n)\nmail.send(msg)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0096","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"What does <code>/retrieve_password</code> return for a known and an unknown email?","a":"<p>A known email returns 200 and the message appears in the Mailtrap inbox. An unknown email returns 401.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"restful-api-f0097","card":"q-restful-api-023-email-with-flask-mail-lost-password","sec":"restful-api-s024","q":"What should production do instead of emailing the password?","a":"<p>Email a secure <strong>reset link</strong> instead of the password, and add rate limiting.</p>","hand":true}];
